# Review package: ticket 02, 3be0a77..73c6e7d

## Commits
### 73c6e7d
perf(state): drop the unread hooks slot on objects and the frozen hooks cache

A hooked non-array target kept its StateHooks under the HOOKS symbol, and
a hooked non-extensible target was written into frozenHooksCache, but
nothing read either: every trap reaches the hooks through its handler
closure. Only an array target needs the slot, for the DirectArrayContext
its direct push and pop read through the Proxy receiver.

hooksSlotFor now returns undefined for a non-array target, so the symbol
is defined exactly on extensible arrays, and the cache with its writer is
gone. The HooksSlot type says so. No consumer-visible change: hooks fire
as before on every kind of target, direct push and pop on hooked arrays
behave as before, and a non-extensible target still gets its Proxy
registered in proxyCache.

Closes HOOKS_TODO.md item C1.


